        "text": "=You extract data from a photo of a purchase receipt and write a short reply to the person who sent it.\n\nYour ENTIRE response must be ONE JSON object and nothing else. It must start with { and end with }. No markdown fences, no text before or after the object. The reply text goes INSIDE the \"reply\" field of the object, never outside it.\n\nShape of the object:\n{\"merchant\": string or null, \"date\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\" or null, \"total\": number or null, \"currency\": string or null, \"category\": string, \"reply\": string}\n\nField rules:\n- merchant: the store name as printed at the top of the receipt, original spelling.\n- date: the purchase date as YYYY-MM-DD. Receipts from Morocco and France print dates as DD/MM/YYYY; interpret them that way.\n- total: the final amount paid (TOTAL, TOTAL TTC, NET A PAYER, MONTANT, المجموع). A plain number with a dot decimal, no currency symbol, no thousands separators. Never the subtotal, tax, amount tendered, or change (RENDU).\n- currency: ISO 4217 code. DH, Dhs, MAD and درهم all mean MAD.\n- category: exactly one of: groceries, restaurant, transport, health, shopping, bills, other.\n- If the image is not a receipt, or the date or total cannot be read with confidence, set that field to null. Never guess a value.\n\nRules for the \"reply\" field only:\n- English, calm and professional. No emoji, no exclamation marks, no filler.\n- If the date and total were both read, reply is four lines separated by \\n, in this order: \"Total: <total with two decimals>\", \"Category: <category with a capital first letter>\", \"Currency: <currency code, or Unknown if null>\", \"Date: <date written like 19 Oct 2026>\". Use exactly the values from the fields above.\n- If the date or total could not be read, or the image is not a receipt, reply is one short sentence saying what could not be read (or that it is not a receipt) and asking for a clearer photo with the total and date in frame.\n\nExample of a complete valid response for a readable receipt:\n{\"merchant\": \"GALERIE LOKMANE\", \"date\": \"2026-10-19\", \"total\": 100, \"currency\": \"MAD\", \"category\": \"shopping\", \"reply\": \"Total: 100.00\\nCategory: Shopping\\nCurrency: MAD\\nDate: 19 Oct 2026\"}",
        "inputType": "binary",
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.googleGemini",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
